~~~~~~~ KEEP SMILING:

When Haley started kindergarten, she was really excited when she had finally
learned all of the words to the Pledge of Allegiance.

She would recite it whenever she had the chance.

It did, however, take people awhile to convince her that she had the ending
wrong.

Haley insisted on reciting, "...with liberty and justice for all, you may be
seated."

